 "best_idea": "Build the to-hit as one named sum clamped to 3..97 and roll it once on the server, and treat a weight-scaled knockback (40 x d^2 / (W + 10 d), floored at 15 classic units) that decays per tick as a client-only push.",
 "decision": "adapt",
 "decision_why": "The server takes the to-hit as a clamped named sum rolled once, which makes hits and kills server-verifiable; the knockback stays a client-only push because the donor applies it to the physics controller and our rulings keep state changes on the server.",
 "decision_status": "proposed",
 "acceptance": "A server test with a fixed seed asserts that a 10-damage hit on a 100-weight target gives a 20-unit classic push that ends after 4 classic updates, and that a chance of 60 hits on roll 59 and misses on roll 60."
}